        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Post-mortem photograph of serial killer Ted Bundy following his execution at the Floria State Prison on January 24th, 1989. Autopsy reports showed the 2,000 volts of electric current scorched Bundy's shaved head and calf, leaving a 7-inch strip of charred skin in both places. \n\nFinding the photo that was on the cover of Weekly World News in 1989 that showed the front of Ted's face and his eyeballs sizzled red like lightning is impossible to find as for some reason that photo has been scrubbed from the internet."
        },
